<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ludwig III of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1845">1845</a>–<a href="/years/1921">1921</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ludwig III was the last king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, reigning from 1913 to 1918. Son of the prince regent Luitpold, he served as regent for his insane cousin Otto from 1912 and then had himself proclaimed king. His support for the German war effort cost him popularity, and when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurt-eisner">Kurt Eisner</a> proclaimed a republic in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a> in November 1918 he fled, ending more than 700 years of Wittelsbach rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ludwig-iii-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Ludwig III of Bavaria" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Library of Congress · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Ludwig,_Bavaria_LOC_29581102430.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
